    "knowledge_point": "Identifying Type II Regions",
    "problem": "Which of the following is a type II region in two-dimensional space?",
    "worked_solution": "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096470/assets/fe16f5f3d1e9663a7e0df88d71639016bfb3357a6745ee6f125968978fd54c12.png)",
